# Giant-Sized Flying Ant has flash (CR 702.8): Bot1 casts it in Bot2's upkeep, {3}{U} paid exactly by Black Lotus's
# {U}{U}{U} and Mox Sapphire's {U}. Its enters trigger is modal (CR 700.2a): Bot1 chooses "Tap target nonland permanent"
# and the target is Bot2's Mox Pearl, not Bot2's Island (a land: the refusal, with the Mox Pearl the positive control).
# As it resolves the Mox Pearl is tapped (CR 701.26a), and stays tapped through the rest of the turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Giant-Sized Flying Ant
Island x4
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Giant-Sized Flying Ant.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
